Lua 5.3.4 (Warcraft III map-runtime dependency)

Source: https://www.lua.org/ftp/lua-5.3.4.tar.gz
SHA-256: f681aa518233bc407e23acf0f5887c884f17436f000d453b2491a9f11a52400c
The supplied 3.0.1.24371 retail executable embeds the Lua 5.3.4 version identity.
This is independent of the existing Lua 5.4.8 WoW UI runtime.

provenance.json records original source hashes and local changes. Five standard
library files append the permanent-function accessors from Eris commit
9d328c612a825ca10f1c495595acd96f27f5e288. lundump.c uses an equivalent explicit
string-index pointer to avoid a current Clang diagnostic. The VM semantics and
standard bytecode layout are otherwise unchanged.

namespace.h maps all 316 external Lua/Eris symbols to bz53_* names. Every
translation unit using this runtime must include namespace.h before Lua headers.
The build force-includes it for the library; consumers include it explicitly.
Regenerate/check with tools/lua53_namespace.py. Drivers lua.c and luac.c are
retained as upstream input but excluded from the archive.

The SDK and heap serializer are covered by make test-lua53. This dependency
alone does not implement Warcraft map loading, native bindings or world saves.
